      "side": 1,
      "message": "Writes to the offset `EC_MEMMAP_BATT_FLAG` are lost, so the ACPI code can\u0027t do anything based on them.\n\nThe following EC code:\n\n```\nvoid set_battery_cutoff(void)\n{\n[[[... Add to EC_MEMMAP_BATT_FLAG ...]]]\n\tuint8_t *memmap_battery_cutoff \u003d\n\t\thost_get_memmap(EC_MEMMAP_BATT_FLAG);\n\t*memmap_battery_cutoff |\u003d EC_BATT_CUT_OFF_ENABLED;\n\n\tCPRINTF(\"TIMTIM \u003e\u003e %s::%d \u003e\u003e *memmap_battery_cutoff \u003d 0x%02X\\n\",\n\t\t__FILE__, __LINE__, *memmap_battery_cutoff);\n\n[[[... New EC_MEMMAP_BATT_CUT_OFF...]]]\n\tmemmap_battery_cutoff \u003d\n\t\thost_get_memmap(EC_MEMMAP_BATT_CUT_OFF);\n\t*memmap_battery_cutoff \u003d 0x1;\n\n\tCPRINTF(\"TIMTIM \u003e\u003e %s::%d \u003e\u003e *memmap_battery_cutoff \u003d 0x%02X\\n\",\n\t\t__FILE__, __LINE__, *memmap_battery_cutoff);\n}\n```\n\nGives this output to the EC console:\n\n```\n22-06-15 12:02:05.515 TIMTIM \u003e\u003e common/battery_v2.c::401 \u003e\u003e *memmap_battery_cutoff \u003d 0x4B\n22-06-15 12:02:05.520 TIMTIM \u003e\u003e common/battery_v2.c::408 \u003e\u003e *memmap_battery_cutoff \u003d 0x01\n```\n\nThe following ACPI code:\n\n```\n[[[ src/ec/google/chromeec/acpi/emem.asl ]]]\nOffset (0x40),\nBTVO, 32,\t// Battery Present Voltage\nBTPR, 32,\t// Battery Present Rate\nBTRA, 32,\t// Battery Remaining Capacity\nACEX, 1,\t// AC Present\nBTEX, 1,\t// Battery Present\nBFDC, 1,\t// Battery Discharging\nBFCG, 1,\t// Battery Charging\nBFCR, 1,\t// Battery Level Critical\nBFIV, 1,\t// Invalid Battery Data\nBFCT, 1,\t// Battery cutoff  \u003c\u003c---- Add to EC_MEMMAP_BATT_FLAG\nOffset (0x4d),\nBTCN, 8,\t// Battery Count\nBTIX, 8,\t// Battery index\nBCUT, 8,\t// Battery cutoff  \u003c\u003c---- New EC_MEMMAP_BATT_CUT_OFF\n```\n\n```\n[[[ SSDT1.dsl ]]]\n    Scope (\\_SB)\n    {\n        Method (DPTC, 0, Serialized)\n        {\n            If (\\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC0.BFCT)\n            {\n                Debug \u003d \"TIMTIM \u003e\u003e BFCT is 1\" \u003c\u003c---- Add to EC_MEMMAP_BATT_FLAG\n            }\n\n            If (\\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC0.BCUT)\n            {\n                Debug \u003d \"TIMTIM \u003e\u003e BCUT is 1\" \u003c\u003c---- New EC_MEMMAP_BATT_CUT_OFF\n            }\n```\n\nGives the following ACPI output:\n\n```\n[  259.784745] ACPI Debug:  \"EC: BATTERY STATUS\"\n[  259.784851] ACPI Debug:  \"ALIB call: func 1 params 0x03 0x00 0x00\"\n[  259.787458] ACPI Debug:  \"TIMTIM \u003e\u003e BCUT is 1\" \u003c\u003c--- New EC_MEMMAP_BATT_CUT_OFF\n[  259.787505] ACPI Debug:  \"DPTC: No/Low battery. Throttling SOC.\"\n```\n\nBased on the above, the block `EC_MEMMAP_BATT_CUT_OFF` is not mutable by `ectool`.   Writing the values \"works\" in that `ectool` can see the updated value, but the mem-mapped block isn\u0027t actually modified so ACPI never sees the updated value.\n\nInstead, creating a new flag at another offset allows ACPI to see the new value and throttle the SOC.\n\nIs there something else I\u0027m missing to allow adding a new flag to `EC_MEMMAP_BATT_FLAG`?",
